From: Ben Schippers <benjamin.schippers@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:47:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?freshness:=20repeat=20alarm=20=E2=80=94=20no=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?slug=20>3=20of=20the=20newest=2010=20receipts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The outside check that the planner's repeat law is holding on the
committed ledger: counts slugs over the newest 10 receipts (same
stamp-degradation rule as the scheduler's own reader, same
REPEAT_HARD_CAP constant) and files/updates a 'windowsill scheduler
repeating' issue when one slug exceeds the cap — the M01-x40 class of
waste pages instead of quietly minting receipts. The feed-stale issue
step is scoped to its own check's outcome so the two alarms cannot
cross-file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/freshness.yml | 70 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 69 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/freshness.yml b/.github/workflows/freshness.yml
index 5d31d35..896cd38 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/freshness.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/freshness.yml
@@ -74,8 +74,76 @@ jobs:
               print(f"::error::feed stale: {detail}")
               sys.exit(1)
           PY
+      # Scheduler repeat alarm — the M01-x40 class of waste. Two 2026-08 bugs
+      # (a stuck open-pointer, then a stem-slice parse livelock) made the lab
+      # re-run one verified rung for days while CI stayed green: 84 of the
+      # first 136 committed receipts were two slugs. The planner's repeat law
+      # (curriculum.REPEAT_HARD_CAP) makes that impossible from inside the
+      # scheduler; this step is the OUTSIDE check that the law is actually
+      # holding on the committed ledger, so the next selection defect pages
+      # instead of quietly minting receipts.
+      - name: no slug dominates the newest receipts (repeat alarm)
+        id: repeats
+        if: always()
+        run: |
+          PYTHONPATH=src python - <<'PY'
+          import collections, json, os, sys
+          from pathlib import Path
+
+          from lab.curriculum import REPEAT_HARD_CAP
+          from lab.publish import _split_receipt_stem
+
+          WINDOW = 10  # newest receipts examined; > REPEAT_HARD_CAP trips
+          ledger = []
+          for path in Path("reports/receipts").glob("run-*.json"):
+              date, _turn, slug = _split_receipt_stem(path.stem[len("run-"):])
+              if not slug:
+                  continue
+              try:
+                  stamp = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")).get("generated_at")
+              except (OSError, ValueError):
+                  stamp = None
+              if not (isinstance(stamp, str) and stamp):
+                  stamp = date  # the ledger's own degradation rule
+              ledger.append((stamp, slug.upper()))
+          newest = [slug for _stamp, slug in sorted(ledger)[-WINDOW:]]
+          counts = collections.Counter(newest)
+          out = open(os.environ["GITHUB_OUTPUT"], "a", encoding="utf-8")
+          if not counts:
+              print("repeat_detail=no receipts on the ledger yet", file=out)
+              sys.exit(0)
+          slug, n = counts.most_common(1)[0]
+          detail = (f"{slug} appears {n}x in the newest {len(newest)} receipts "
+                    f"(alarm threshold >{REPEAT_HARD_CAP}): {' '.join(newest)}")
+          print(f"repeat_detail={detail}", file=out)
+          print(detail)
+          if n > REPEAT_HARD_CAP:
+              print(f"::error::scheduler repeating: {detail}")
+              sys.exit(1)
+          PY
+      - name: Create or update the "windowsill scheduler repeating" issue
+        if: always() && steps.repeats.outcome == 'failure'
+        env:
+          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
+          GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}
+          DETAIL: ${{ steps.repeats.outputs.repeat_detail }}
+          RUN_URL: ${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs/${{ github.run_id }}
+        run: |
+          title="windowsill scheduler repeating"
+          body="${DETAIL:-repeat alarm failed before counting the ledger}
+
+          - run: ${RUN_URL}
+
+          The planner's repeat law (value × 2^-repeats, hard cap ${REPEAT_CAP:-3}) should make this impossible from inside \`lab next\` — so if this fired, either a box is running with a broken planner fallback loop or receipts are landing outside the scheduler. First moves: \`lab next --dry-run\` on each box and read the newest receipts' \`planned\` blocks in \`reports/receipts/\`."
+          num=$(gh issue list --state open --json number,title \
+                --jq '[.[] | select(.title == "windowsill scheduler repeating")][0].number // empty')
+          if [ -n "$num" ]; then
+            gh issue comment "$num" --body "$body"
+          else
+            gh issue create --title "$title" --body "$body"
+          fi
       - name: Create or update the "windowsill feed stale" issue
-        if: failure()
+        if: always() && steps.age.outcome == 'failure'
         env:
           GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
           GH_REPO: ${{ github.repository }}
